Forgets a custom geometry tile when it's cancelled, as the custom vector loader
already does, so the tile fetches again when it is next required. Before, the
source told the provider to cancel the tile and never asked for it again
(https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native-ffi/issues/778).
Upstream: not proposed

diff --git a/src/mln/style/custom_tile_loader.cpp b/src/mln/style/custom_tile_loader.cpp
index a7e306c..6b2d590 100644
--- a/src/mln/style/custom_tile_loader.cpp
+++ b/src/mln/style/custom_tile_loader.cpp
@@ -38,6 +38,8 @@ void CustomTileLoader::cancelTile(const OverscaledTileID& tileID) {
     std::scoped_lock guard(dataMutex);
     if (tileCallbackMap.contains(tileID.canonical)) {
         invokeTileCancel(tileID.canonical);
+        // Erase so a subsequent fetchTile for the same tile re-issues the fetch.
+        tileCallbackMap.erase(tileID.canonical);
     }
 }
 
